254
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,697
That caused a short circuit,

255
00:20:06,780 --> 00:20:10,251
and the surge from that caused
a spike in the STL's output.

256
00:20:11,420 --> 00:20:15,600
As a result, Kirito's self-destructive
impulse was actualized.

257
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:18,797
Then, his ego was...

258
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:19,940
deactivated.

259
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:21,660
I don't get it.

260
00:20:21,820 --> 00:20:23,620
His ego was deactivated?

261
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:25,742
I didn't know that was possible.

262
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:27,649
Have a look at the screen.

263
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:29,837
That's a Fluctlight.

264
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:31,957
Kirito's Fluctlight, to be precise.

265
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:36,440
And that black hole right there is
where a person's self-image should be.

266
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:38,637
The self-image?

267
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:41,700
The idea, concept, or
mental image of oneself?

268
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,070
Yep.

269
00:20:43,153 --> 00:20:45,157
All of your decision-making passes through

270
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:47,780
a simple yes-no pathway
in your Fluctlight.

271
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:50,837
It asks whether you should
or shouldn't do something,

272
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:52,737
based on whatever situation you're in.

273
00:20:52,820 --> 00:20:54,560
For example, Dr.

274
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:59,484
Kojiro, when you're at your fave beef bowl
place, you ever order a second helping?

275
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:00,790
No.

276
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:05,537
Even if in your mind you're like, damn,
this is good, I could eat another bowl.

277
00:21:05,620 --> 00:21:06,450
Never.

278
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:08,777
And that's your self-image
pathway at work.

279
00:21:08,860 --> 00:21:12,337
Decisions can't lead to actions
unless they go through those circuits.

280
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:16,340
In Kirito's case, his Fluctlight
is damaged in that one spot.

281
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:20,237
He can't process what happens around
him and he can't initiate an action.

282
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:24,180
All he can do, I think, is stuff
he remembers from repetition.

283
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:26,620
Eating, sleeping, stuff like that.

284
00:21:29,060 --> 00:21:32,884
Right now, I don't think he knows
who he is or what he should do.

285
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,647
And he can't speak, so
he can't ask for help.

286
00:21:35,860 --> 00:21:37,389
But that's just my theory.

287
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:05,360
I'm sorry.

288
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:13,657
It's so sad that it's

289
00:22:13,740 --> 00:22:16,840
so sad that it's so sad.

290
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:20,380
I can't live alone alone.

291
00:22:26,100 --> 00:22:30,680
I don't want anyone to love you?

292
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:36,540
I don't know how much I can do it.

293
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:40,880
It's your story.

294
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:45,320
It's my body.

295
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:48,900
It's my love.

296
00:22:51,260 --> 00:22:53,300
My goal.

297
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:32,060
I'm not going to die.

298
00:23:36,140 --> 00:23:38,060
Next time, the final test.
